Subject: [PATCH 337/371] pirates: Seven Card Stud tables in Port Royal tavern
 2 and Tortuga tavern 1 (7stud-0001, AI only)

Seven Card Stud had its client class, AI class, DC Distributed7StudTable and Lookout wiring, but the world data placed
no 7 Stud table, so nobody could sit at one. The lone parlor table in port_royal_building_int_tavern_2 and in
tortuga_building_int_tavern changes 'Category': 'Holdem' -> '7Stud' (an original value: the editor's own Category list
in ObjectList.py is Blackjack / Holdem / 7Stud). Each town keeps a Holdem table in its other tavern. Counts after:
Blackjack 12, Holdem 8, 7Stud 2. Same table prop, cards and chips as Holdem; no client change.

AI restart only (world data is read when the AI builds the interior). Test: test_7stud.py (real createParlorTable +
a dealt hand: 7 cards over 5 streets, no community cards; Holdem control): live FAIL 22/23 -> patched PASS 23/23.
The 7 Stud AI has not run a live hand yet; one bot hand at the table is the live check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
